A||N||8||flyntus||Ed Parks/Fiero Factory Visit||||7||
Z||000000||flyntus||10-29-2001||09:34 PM||||I would like to tell everyone about the great time I had dropping my '85 SE off at Ed Parks & the Fiero Factory this past Friday. I'm having Ed replace all suspension parts to include 1" lowering springs, new shocks, bushings, etc AND install 3.4 engine  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Everyone there were knowledgeable & very friendly like the Fiero family they are.  I don't mind telling you that Rosie knows more about Fieros than I do. To see 10 4.9's still in crates is a sight to behold. Too bad I couldn't get Ed to put one in my car.  I did get a chance to see the Blue Taz with its 4.9 engine, what a BEAUTIFUL car!  Ed has a beautiful white 88 Formula he said he was interested in selling. I hope to pick my car up in about 2 weeks. Will let you know when I get her back.||||reg||7
Z||000001||terryk||10-29-2001||10:26 PM||||Hey, I was just there a week ago Friday. I hung out with Jeremy for a bit. Got the grand tour and complementary "Breakfast with the Cast"....<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000002||qwikgta||10-29-2001||10:44 PM||||Does Ed have a website or an email address.<P>Thanks<P>Rob||||reg||1
Z||000003||flyntus||10-29-2001||10:54 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by qwikgta:<BR><B>Does Ed have a website or an email address.<P>Thanks<P>Rob</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Rob,<BR>Go to <A HREF="http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top" TARGET=_blank>http://www.angelfire.com/on/fierofactory/start.html#top</A> <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000004||MooCow||10-29-2001||10:56 PM||||yes I have been there 3 times now.  I love going.  I had Ed put in a 3.4 into my car.  Did you get a change to drive the white coupe that he had?&gt;?  That car got me hooked on the 4:10 trans for a 3.4.  Yes Taz's car is awsome looking.  He used to have a 3800 in there but now the 4.9 like you said.  I am going to be going again soon, as soon as Ed finally has the 4.9 all done and ready to become a kit to try it out.  And yes Rosie is full of knowledge when is comes to Fiero's.  Anyone who goes there will have a blast.  I took so many pics when I was there.<P>Thanks Ken||||reg||10
Z||000005||flyntus||10-29-2001||11:09 PM||||I did have a chance to drive Ed's coupe, I wanted to go with the 4.10 but the financial side of what's left of my brain took over & I'll stick with my 3.68.  After seeing the Blue TAZ, so many things I want to do, so little money.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||10-29-2001||11:22 PM||||flyntus, if you don't mind me asking, how much does the 3.4 conversion cost? Are you providing the 2.8 and 3.4? Or is your Fiero a 2.5?<P>I'm interested within the next year or so putting a 3.4 in my SE. Think of it, a 3.4L turbo Fiero! WOW<BR>It's already fast enough for me!<BR>Thanks!!||||reg||1
Z||000007||tgowens||10-30-2001||12:08 AM||||terryk, ya gotta watch out for Jeremy!! He's a great guy but when he drives that truck of his into the shop ya better watch out!! It is so lowered it almost can't make it into the bay!! And, he comes in at about 70 miles an hour!!<P>And, you all think Rosie knows a lot about Fieros? Just where do you think Ed learned what he knows??  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>They are a good buch of people though, Ed, Rosie, Jeremy, Rick and Dave -- they all know what they are doing (which is more than I can say for myself!!)<P>------------------<BR><A HREF="http://www.whgraphics.com" TARGET=_blank>West Highland Graphics & Design</A><BR><A HREF="http://www.cfog-i.org" TARGET=_blank>Classic Fiero Owners Group International</A>||||reg||1
Z||000008||cadero2dmax||10-30-2001||12:27 AM||||Ed also hosts his Swap Meet annually the last weekend in April. The last year (April 2000) the Fiero Racing List presented him with the "Fiero Factory" sign out front on the highway and I had my Quad 4 powered 1900 pound racer on display. Couldn't make it this year, but the 2002 meet will have the Challenge car, among other displays.<P>It is well worth the time and effort, and it is HUGE - - you will meet Fiero nuts from all over the place, besides having an opportunity to pick up just about any part there is for your car.<P><P>------------------<BR>G<BR>Daily Driver - <BR>85 SE<BR>4.9 Cad<BR>Isuzu 5 speed<BR>'88 cradle<BR>lowered 2 1/2"<BR>Mr. Mikes interior<P>GRM $2002 Challenge Fiero<BR>84 coupe<BR>4.9 (carburated)<BR>2.86:1 TH-125 w/shift kit||||reg||1
